From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Bruno=20Greg=C3=B3rio?= <accounts@bruno.pw>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 09:04:49 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: Add SM6450 SoC device tree
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add the base device tree for SM6450: eight CPUs in one cluster (four
Cortex-A55 and four Cortex-A78) with their idle states and PSCI power
domains, the carve-outs the firmware owns, GCC, TLMM, the GIC, PDC,
IPCC, the TCSR mutex, the memory-mapped timer, the APSS watchdog, the
RPMh RSC with its clock and power domain controllers, the EPSS CPU
frequency controller, the QUPv3 wrapper holding the debug UART, the
SPMI arbiter with both its buses, the AOSS side channel and its sleep
stats, and SMEM with the four SMP2P edges that ride on it.

Signed-off-by: Bruno Gregório <accounts@bruno.pw>
---
